.TH WMMONITORS 1 "November 2026" "Window Maker"
.SH NAME
wmmonitors \- configure monitors using a WINGs layout editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmmonitors
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmmonitors
shows connected RandR outputs as movable rectangles with background previews.
Drag a rectangle to place a monitor to the left, right, above or below another.
Nearby edges snap together. Overlapping rectangles are allowed.
Click the star or its "primary" label at the bottom-left of a monitor to make it primary.
The primary monitor has a gold star; other monitors have gray stars.
If RandR has no explicit primary, the star marks Window Maker's default first
enabled monitor.
Use each monitor's bottom-right checkbox or its "active" label to enable or disable it.
Disabled monitors appear as dimmed cards in a tray inside the canvas,
where their checkboxes can enable them again.
Use the tray arrows or mouse wheel to browse additional disabled monitors.
Mirrored monitors are drawn as stacked cards with individually exposed controls.
At least one output must remain enabled.
.PP
Right-click a rectangle to open its resolution, refresh rate, rotation and
reflection controls. Unsupported rotation and reflection choices are disabled.
Active backgrounds are read from the desktop background pixmap; new or disabled
outputs use their saved Window Maker background, or the default background color.
Saved-texture previews support solid colors, two-color gradients and image
textures; other texture types use the default color and produce a warning.
.PP
Plugging or unplugging a monitor, or an external layout change, reloads the live
configuration and discards staged edits. Scaling transforms and panning must be
reset with
.B xrandr
before applying layouts in this editor.
.SH APPLYING AND SAVING
.B Apply
changes the current X-server configuration, not the startup configuration.
Choose
.B Keep
within 15 seconds to confirm, or the previous layout is restored.
.B Revert
restores it immediately. Closing during confirmation also reverts.
If monitors are unplugged during confirmation, the old snapshot cannot be
restored safely; the editor reloads the available outputs and reports this.
.PP
.B Save Layout
stores the confirmed live layout in the GNUstep defaults file
.BR WMMonitorLayout .
.B Load Layout
stages the saved layout for review; it does not activate it.
Outputs are matched by connector name, and modes by name and refresh rate,
not by X-server resource identifiers.
Missing monitors are ignored, and newly attached monitors retain their live
settings. Unavailable saved modes and invalid layouts are reported as errors.
Nothing is automatically restored at login.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-display " display"
Select the X display.
.TP
.BR \-\-help " | " \-h
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version " | " \-v
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/GNUstep/Defaults/WMMonitorLayout
Saved monitor configuration. WMAKER_USER_ROOT can relocate the GNUstep directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR WPrefs (1),
.BR wmwallpaper (1),
.BR wmsetbg (1),
.BR xrandr (1)
